/target

# The sandbox writes its Claude Code configuration, session history and OAuth
# credentials into .sbx/, so the directory is ignored by default and the kit is
# named back in. Ignoring the contents rather than the directory itself is what
# lets the negation take effect: git does not descend into an excluded directory.
# The same rule is why .sbx/ is named back in first: a user's global ignore file
# may exclude the directory outright, and a pattern here beats one from there.
!/.sbx
/.sbx/*
!/.sbx/kit
